# Ford Puma three-door coupe, 1997-2002.
#
# The original Puma: the Fiesta-based four-seat coupe with the rounded New
# Edge styling, the long bonnet and the curved rear haunch. UK sales from
# mid-July 1997, at first with the 1.7 only; the 1.4 followed in February 1998
# and the 1.6 in October 2000. Not to be confused with the 2019 Puma
# crossover, which shares only the name.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Puma
#
# Dimensions 3.984 x 1.674 x 1.345 m, wheelbase 2.445 m.
#
# Shape reference: the side photograph is square in yaw within about 5
# degrees but the camera is 10-15 degrees above the centre line, so the roof
# and bonnet tops show and the flank is a close estimate rather than an
# orthographic trace. The car is Spanish-registered.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK colour list was read. Blue, Red, Silver and Black
# are plain names. Weights 14, 12, 10, 8, total 44, provisional.
#
# Speed 200 km/h. Comfort 65/428, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 65. Classes 1,2.
# Dates: intro July 1997; retires staggered 2013-2016 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-puma-1997.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/ford-puma-1997.dae. References:
# citycars/references/ford-puma-1997/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the flank is a close estimate from a near-broadside
# photograph taken about 10-15 degrees above the centre line, with the nose
# partly obscured. The rear lamp internals, the deck-lip contours and the
# intake detail are simplified.


